; xgold.tech — the records Squarespace served on 2026-10-20, in BIND format for
; Cloudflare → DNS → Records → Import. Import with "Proxy imported records" UNCHECKED so every
; record arrives DNS-only (grey cloud) and the cutover changes nothing but the nameservers.
;
;   @ / www / fam      GitHub Pages (cartergloyd.github.io) — the owner's sites
;   api.fam / streaming / mc   the home IP (port-forwarded services; the VPN has exceptions for them)
;   _minecraft._tcp.mc  SRV so clients find the Java server without a port
;   TXT                 "no mail is sent from this domain" (SPF -all, DMARC reject, empty DKIM)
;
; NOT included: _domainconnect CNAME → _domainconnect.domains.squarespace.com — Squarespace's
; Domain Connect only works while Squarespace serves DNS; delete it from the Cloudflare zone.
;
; After the cutover the tunnel adds its own records: fam-api, ai-api (later dash) are proxied
; CNAMEs to <tunnel-id>.cfargotunnel.com, added as routes of the tunnel (SERVER_SETUP § 5.2).
; The api.fam A record below is the legacy pre-tunnel API host — delete it once nothing uses it.
; mc / streaming MUST stay DNS-only: Minecraft and Jellyfin are not HTTP on 80/443 and the
; Cloudflare proxy would break them. The audit's [dns] section checks exactly this.

$ORIGIN xgold.tech.
$TTL 14400

@                     14400 IN A      185.199.108.153
@                     14400 IN A      185.199.109.153
@                     14400 IN A      185.199.110.153
@                     14400 IN A      185.199.111.153
www                   14400 IN CNAME  cartergloyd.github.io.
fam                   14400 IN CNAME  cartergloyd.github.io.

api.fam                3600 IN A      99.116.141.110
mc                     3600 IN A      99.116.141.110
streaming             14400 IN A      99.116.141.110
_minecraft._tcp.mc     3600 IN SRV    0 5 25565 mc.xgold.tech.

@                     14400 IN TXT    "v=spf1 -all"
_dmarc                14400 IN TXT    "v=DMARC1; p=reject; sp=reject; adkim=s; aspf=s"
_domainkey            14400 IN TXT    "v=DKIM1; p="
